  "featureGroup": false,
  "description": "The \u0027dss_users_cached\u0027 dataset provides comprehensive information about user accounts within a system, focusing on login credentials, user profiles, and activity tracking. This dataset is crucial for managing user access and monitoring engagement within the platform. It includes key identifiers such as login emails and display names, which are essential for user identification and communication. The dataset also details user profiles and group memberships, which define the access levels and permissions for each user. Additionally, it tracks the origin of user accounts, whether local or otherwise, and includes timestamps for account creation, last successful login, and last session activity, providing insights into user engagement and system usage patterns. The \u0027enabled\u0027 column indicates whether a user account is active, which is vital for security and user management. Furthermore, the dataset includes URLs for user management interfaces, facilitating administrative tasks. This dataset is particularly useful for system administrators and security teams to ensure efficient user management, access control, and to enhance the overall security posture of the platform.",
  "shortDesc": "User account dataset with login, profile, and activity details.",
